WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.151
<v Contracts Supervisor>Thanks for making time. The senior grants specialist starts leave

00:00:03.151 --> 00:00:06.303
<v Contracts Supervisor>in three months. I want to talk about what you

00:00:06.303 --> 00:00:07.248
<v Contracts Supervisor>might take on.

00:00:07.598 --> 00:00:11.158
<v Grants Specialist>Honestly, I assumed you would give it to the newer

00:00:11.158 --> 00:00:14.006
<v Grants Specialist>specialist. They are always the first to volunteer.

00:00:14.356 --> 00:00:16.865
<v Contracts Supervisor>I will be honest too. I did assume you were

00:00:16.865 --> 00:00:19.374
<v Contracts Supervisor>not interested. You have not asked for new work in

00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:19.876
<v Contracts Supervisor>a while.

00:00:20.226 --> 00:00:23.930
<v Grants Specialist>I stopped asking. I asked twice for the complex agreements

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:27.635
<v Grants Specialist>a few years ago, under a different supervisor, and nothing

00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:28.746
<v Grants Specialist>came of it.

00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:32.386
<v Contracts Supervisor>That helps me understand. Research on coaching finds supervisors tend

00:00:32.386 --> 00:00:35.677
<v Contracts Supervisor>to invest in people they already see as engaged. I

00:00:35.677 --> 00:00:38.967
<v Contracts Supervisor>may have been doing that. What would you want to

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:39.296
<v Contracts Supervisor>learn?

00:00:39.646 --> 00:00:43.570
<v Grants Specialist>The multi-year agreements with the larger providers. I know the

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:47.494
<v Grants Specialist>monitoring side well. I have never built the budget pieces.

00:00:47.844 --> 00:00:51.088
<v Contracts Supervisor>Then let's stage it. You build the budget for the

00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:54.333
<v Contracts Supervisor>next renewal, with the senior specialist reviewing each week. Not

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.604
<v Contracts Supervisor>all of the complex work at once.

00:00:56.954 --> 00:00:59.882
<v Grants Specialist>Why not all at once? I can handle it.

00:01:00.232 --> 00:01:03.443
<v Contracts Supervisor>I think you can. One study of managers found that

00:01:03.443 --> 00:01:06.654
<v Contracts Supervisor>learning grows with challenge but levels off when it gets

00:01:06.654 --> 00:01:09.864
<v Contracts Supervisor>too steep, unless feedback is built in. I want you

00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:12.112
<v Contracts Supervisor>to keep learning, not just keep up.

00:01:12.462 --> 00:01:16.022
<v Grants Specialist>That is fair. I would need something taken off my

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:18.870
<v Grants Specialist>plate. The monitoring cycle is heavy right now.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.700
<v Contracts Supervisor>I will move two monitoring visits to the newer specialist.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.180
<v Contracts Supervisor>They want to learn monitoring anyway. After each budget review,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:29.660
<v Contracts Supervisor>could you and I do a short debrief, fifteen minutes,

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.444
<v Contracts Supervisor>on what worked and what you would change?

00:01:32.794 --> 00:01:35.939
<v Grants Specialist>Yes. And I would like this in my development plan.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:38.770
<v Grants Specialist>I want to be ready for a senior role.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.375
<v Contracts Supervisor>Let's write it now. One assignment, the renewal budget. One

00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:47.631
<v Contracts Supervisor>skill, multi-year budgeting. One support, weekly review with the senior

00:01:47.631 --> 00:01:50.184
<v Contracts Supervisor>specialist. Let's revisit it every month.
